WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.968
Host: Why can adding enzyme accelerate a
reaction without changing its final
equilibrium?

2
00:00:05.968 --> 00:00:11.397
Guide: Catalysis lowers the kinetic barrier
for forward and reverse reaction paths.

3
00:00:11.397 --> 00:00:15.086
Guide: It changes how quickly equilibrium is
reached,

4
00:00:15.086 --> 00:00:19.359
Guide: not the relative free energies of
reactants and products.

5
00:00:19.359 --> 00:00:26.643
Host: In a simple reversible competitive-
inhibition model, what can increasing
substrate concentration do?

6
00:00:26.643 --> 00:00:33.341
Guide: Reduce the inhibitor's effect on the
observed rate. Substrate competes for binding;

7
00:00:33.341 --> 00:00:38.760
Guide: sufficiently high substrate can
approach the same Vmax in the ideal model.
